  <h2 id='reserving'>10.3 Reserving space honestly</h2>
  <p>
    A reservation is a promise about the future: the container claims the space its content will
    need. The strategies, in order of preference:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Exact dimensions, when the content's size is knowable.</strong> A paginated table with 10
      rows of 44px is 440px before any data exists: rows-per-page times row height <em>is</em> the reservation.
      Media is the canonical case: always give images explicit <code>width</code>/<code>height</code
      > (or <code>aspect-ratio</code>) so the browser reserves before loading; <code
        >next/image</code
      > enforces this.
      <Chip k='react' />
      <Chip k='critical' />
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>min-height</code>, when only the floor is knowable.</strong> Reserve the minimum honest
      footprint: enough that the common case doesn't shift, growth is rare and downward. A dishonest reservation
      (a token 40px under a region that always renders 400px) is just a smaller earthquake.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Flex-grow and scroll, for the main content region.</strong> The strongest reservation is
      the viewport itself: the page frame is a column that clips itself (<code
        >h-full max-h-full overflow-hidden</code
      >): header and toolbars sized by content, the content region growing (<code>grow</code>) with
      <code>overflow-y: auto</code>. The page as a whole <em>never changes height</em>; tables can
      grow, filters can change the row count, and all of it happens inside a scroll area whose outer
      box is fixed. This is the default posture for every list/table page in the app. <Chip
        k='react'
      />
      <Chip k='very' />
    </li>
  </ul>

  <Snippet>
    <pre
      class='code v-good'
      is:raw><span class="filename">app/(admin)/reports/layout.tsx - the flex-grow-and-scroll frame</span><span class="tok-kw">export default function</span> <span class="tok-fn">ReportsLayout</span>({ children }) {
  <span class="tok-kw">return</span> (
    <span class="tok-com">{/* The column is exactly viewport height; the page never grows. */}</span>
    &lt;div <span class="tok-prop">className</span>=<span class="tok-str">"flex h-full max-h-full overflow-hidden flex-col"</span>&gt;
      &lt;<span class="tok-fn">ReportsHeader</span> /&gt;
      <span class="tok-com">{/* The content region takes the remainder and scrolls inside.
          Whatever streams, loads, or grows in here, the frame holds. */}</span>
      &lt;main <span class="tok-prop">className</span>=<span class="tok-str">"min-h-0 grow overflow-y-auto"</span>&gt;
        {children}
      &lt;/main&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  );
}</pre>
  </Snippet>

