      The sibling version of the previous figure. The routes are peers with different paths, yet the
      header, the tab bar, and the content container belong to the <code>(program)</code> group's layout,
      so a navigation between them re-renders only the page inside; the active-tab highlight comes from
      a tiny <code>useSelectedLayoutSegment</code> leaf, not from re-rendering the bar. The two pages
      even hold different shapes, a table for learners and a detail card for evaluators, and still the
      frame never moves. The wrong version repeats the header and tabs inside each sibling's page file,
      and every navigation tears down and rebuilds the exact chrome the user is staring at.
